WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.183
Week 1: How Spanish Works. spell a name recognize a stressed syllable build a sustainable study loop

2
00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:29.399
Read for the situation. Ana abre su cuaderno. Escucha una palabra, marca la sílaba fuerte y la repite. No busca la perfección; busca una mejora clara cada día. Ana opens her notebook. She listens to a word, marks the stressed syllable, and repeats it. She is not seeking perfection; she seeks one clear improvement each day.

3
00:00:29.399 --> 00:00:38.161
Read again for evidence. Identify who acts, what changes, when it happens, and which words establish the relationship between events.

4
00:00:38.161 --> 00:00:43.403
Reading activities. Reading activity 1; Reading activity 2

5
00:00:43.403 --> 00:00:51.397
Retell. Without looking back, give the main idea, three supporting details, and one reasonable inference in Spanish.

6
00:00:51.397 --> 00:01:18.401
Model language. Mi nombre se escribe con cinco letras. — My name is spelled with five letters. La h no tiene sonido. — The letter h has no sound. Escucho y repito cada palabra. — I listen to and repeat every word. ¿Cuál es la sílaba tónica? — Which is the stressed syllable? La práctica breve y frecuente funciona mejor. — Brief, frequent practice works better.

7
00:01:18.401 --> 00:01:28.555
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
